# cn() conditional classes: use object notation

When using `cn()` for conditional classes, always use object notation instead of logical AND (`&&`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
className={cn('base-classes', isActive && 'active-class')}

// ✅ GOOD
className={cn('base-classes', { 'active-class': isActive })}
```
